+Quoted values (`"..."` or `'...'`) have their quotes removed, and a `#` preceded by whitespace starts a trailing comment on an unquoted value.
+
+## Checking the configuration
+
+`python -m payhook doctor` prints every setting with its effective value and where it came from (`env`, `.env` or `default`), plus the path of the `.env` file it looked for. Paste its output into support tickets. Secrets (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are masked to their last four characters; the full values are never printed.
+
+`python -m payhook check` lists missing required settings and exits non-zero if any are missing.
+
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest`.
